To make the suit faster and more agile in tight aerial maneuvers, Tony redesigned the boots and calves with expanded leg stabilization guards. This reinforced leg structure allowed the Mark X to sustain higher G-force turns and sudden stops without putting strain on the pilot. While retaining the classic red-and-gold color scheme, it served as an important testbed for the flight technology that Tony would later refine in his high-speed interceptor armors. It answered the call during the House Party Protocol battle before being destroyed alongside the rest of the Iron Legion when Tony ordered JARVIS to initiate "Clean Slate."
